  "question": {
    "text": "Depression in freezing point of 0.01 molal aqueous HCOOH solution is 0.02046°C. 1 molal aqueous urea solution freezes at –1.86°C. Assuming molality equal to molarity, calculate the pH of HCOOH solution."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "3.00",
  "solution": {
    "text": "1.86 = K<sub>f</sub>(1)<br /><br />0.02046 = (1 + <math> <mtext>α</mtext></math>) × 1.86 × 0.01<br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mo>⇒</mo><mn>1</mn> <mo>+</mo> <mtext>α</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>0</mn> <mtext>.</mtext> <mn>0</mn> <mn>2</mn> <mn>0</mn> <mn>4</mn> <mn>6</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>0</mn> <mtext>.</mtext> <mn>0</mn> <mn>1</mn> <mn>8</mn> <mn>6</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>=</mo> <mn>1</mn> <mtext>.</mtext> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> </math><br /><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo><mtext> α</mtext> </math> = 0.1<br /><br />[H<sup>+</sup>] = C<math> <mtext>α</mtext> </math> = 0.01 × 0.1 = 10<sup>–3</sup><br /><br />so, pH = 3."
  }
}